"""
Paper XGBoost — Rolling Calibration Training Script
=====================================================
Replicates the Barnor, Kampouridis & Kanellopoulos (2026) XGBoost methodology
for French NUTS-2 regions with rolling yearly calibration.

Pipeline (per region, per calibration year):
  1. Load DAT from region_avg.csv, remove Feb 29, impute missing (Eqs 6-8)
  2. OLS linear detrending (§3.1.1)
  3. Fourier deseasonalization (Berhane et al. 2021)
  4. Feature engineering (Table 2)
  5. Nested CV: 5 outer × 3 inner, HalvingGridSearchCV (§3.2.2)
  6. Refit best model on full calibration data
  7. Save PKL with everything needed for recursive walk-forward forecasting

Rolling calibration:
  calib through 2014-12-31 → predicts 2015
  calib through 2015-12-31 → predicts 2016
  ...
  calib through 2023-12-31 → predicts 2024

Output PKLs saved to: EXPORT_DIR / paper_xgb_region_{R}_calib_{Y}.pkl
Each PKL contains:
  - fitted_model:    XGBRegressor with best hyperparameters
  - scaler:          fitted StandardScaler
  - trend_intercept: OLS intercept
  - trend_slope:     OLS slope
  - fourier_coefs:   fitted Fourier regression coefficients
  - n_harmonics:     number of Fourier harmonics used
  - best_params:     best hyperparameters from nested CV
  - region:          region code
  - calib_year:      calibration year
  - calib_end_tidx:  last t_idx in calibration (for extending trend to test)
  - n_train_days:    number of training days (for t_idx computation)
  - training_df:     last 5 years of processed training data (for create_feat)

Usage:
  python paper_xgboost_rolling_train.py
"""

